#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# rotate_right

#% text
# `rotate_right(xs)` cycles the elements of `xs` one place to the right; `rotate_right(xs, k)` cycles them `k` places.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
rotate_right([1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= [4, 1, 2, 3]

#% cell
rotate_right([1, 2, 3, 4], 3)
#% output
#= [2, 3, 4, 1]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Rotating by the length gives the list back:

#% cell
rotate_right([a, b, c], 3)
#% output
#= [a, b, c]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `rotate_left`, `reverse`
